  "answer": "To handle errors and raise HTTP exceptions in FastAPI, you can override the default exception handlers. This can be done by importing the `HTTPException` from `fastapi` and using it to decorate your exception handler. For example, you can override the default JSON response for `HTTPException` errors by creating a custom exception handler. Additionally, you can handle request validation exceptions by importing `RequestValidationError` and using it with `@app.exception_handler(RequestValidationError)`. This allows you to customize the error responses and provide more detailed information to the client. [tutorial/handling-errors-9] [tutorial/handling-errors-8] [deployment/concepts-14] [tutorial/handling-errors-7] [reference/exceptions-0]",
